scope: |
  Size the RESIDUAL of SSC3-J4 before building anything, which is what the row itself demands
  ("the payoff is COUNTED before the pass is written").

  Both shapes of the §10.2 census have already shipped as ordinary IR->IR passes — the const
  half as J4a (loop-invariant hoist) and the cmp-branch half as J4b (invert, drop the `not`) —
  so the open row is partly stale. §10.2 predicted a floor of 4/9/6 dispatches per loop body
  for arith-loop/nested-loop/list-fold; the landed passes report 5/12/6-7. The question is
  whether that gap justifies the fusion machinery and its representation fork.

  WIDENED to v3/src/Specialize.scala: counting post-optimization needs a printer for the
  OPTIMIZED module and none exists — `SpecializeMain` prints the specialized one and
  `--census` gives whole-module totals, not per-loop-body. Adding `--optimized` beside the
  existing `--census` is the instrument, in the file that already carries that instrument.
next: print the optimized module, count loop bodies, compare with the 10.2 floor
